# DESK13 run C -- the copy confirmation (`ADCPYDEL`), both answers.
#
# Alt+C opens C:\; double-clicking DESKT13 (431,105) opens C:\DESKT13\ in a
# second window (staggered at 72,67). ONE.TXT is the first icon of that
# window, centre (118,130); the C: desktop icon is visible left of both
# windows at (32,42) -- dropping a window selection there is `fun_file2desk`'s
# AT_ISDISK arm, i.e. a copy into C:\.
#
# TIMING (first attempt failed here): the injector steps once per `pump_input`,
# i.e. once per idle pass of the AES event loop. A `down` immediately followed
# by the drag packets is answered by `evnt_multi` only after both have been
# fed, so the desktop saw the press at the *drop* point. The press therefore
# dwells ~3 s at the source and the drag is walked in three hops.
#
# The box is 320x180, so `form_center` puts it at ((640-320)/2,
# 19+(480-19-180)/2) = (160,159); OK (24,128,90,28) -> (229,301),
# Cancel (206,128) -> (411,301).
